  "prompt": "What penalties apply to late filing of a VAT return?",
  "runtimeCommit": "1b36eeadb26d69f2b9ae28c8422afcc3fdd5c6d2",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nPenalties for late filing of a VAT return include a fine of PHP 1,000 and an additional penalty of 25% of the amount due, as stipulated in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provisions are found in the NIRC, specifically:\n- **Section 248**: This section outlines the penalties for failure to file returns and pay taxes, including the fines and surcharges applicable for late filings.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, if a VAT-registered taxpayer fails to file their return by the due date, they will incur an immediate fine of PHP 1,000. Furthermore, if there is any tax due that remains unpaid, the taxpayer will face an additional financial burden of 25% of that amount. This can significantly increase the total liability, making timely filing crucial for compliance and financial management.",
